[center][size=6][b]TheExpanse[/b][/size]
[size=4]Companion mod for the MCRN Corvette ships[/size]
[size=3]A mod for Hardspace: Shipbreaker · v0.7.1[/size][/center]

[line]

A small companion to the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/hardspaceshipbreaker/mods/41]MCRN Corvette[/url] (the Tachi, the Rocinante and the Beratnas Gas Hauler). It handles things that come from how those ships are designed and built, and makes their ghost-ship version properly haunted. The ships play without it; they play better with it.

The game's own ships are not changed.


[size=5][b]The fusion torch drive has to be shut down safely[/b][/size]
The MCRN Corvette runs on a Solomon Epstein torch drive. Its core is a pulsing ball of fusion plasma in the reactor chamber, fed by eight plasma injectors around it. Each live injector feeds it through a containment beam. Before you can salvage the reactor, take the injectors off one at a time.

[size=4][b]How to shut it down[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]Pick an injector[/b] (which one depends on the mode, below).
[*][b]Wait until the three red lights on its handle are all dark.[/b] They sync on the core's beat, like the game's breaker panels.
[*][b]Use the handle while they are dark.[/b] Its beam goes out: that injector is done.
[*][b]Repeat[/b] until all eight are out. The core shrinks and fades away.
[/list]
Pull a handle while its lights are lit and the plasma flashes back: you catch fire. You can also cut the purple pipe running up from an injector to the reactor's lid (freeze it first); that is never timed.

[size=4][b]Watch the core's color[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#8cbeff][b]Blue[/b][/color]: all good.
[*][color=#ff8c28][b]Orange[/b][/color]: level 1, something is off.
[*][color=#ff2814][b]Red[/b][/color]: level 2, unstable. A warning beep sounds in your helmet.
[*][color=#be32ff][b]Purple[/b][/color]: level 3. EVACUATE! A burst of plasma will destroy every injector and the reactor starts to melt down. [b]Run.[/b]
[/list]
Leave a problem alone and the core goes up a level by itself; the beep speeds up just before it does. Fix it and the core goes back to blue.

[size=4][b]Three types of challenges to shut it down[/b][/size]
Each ship picks two of the nav terminals on the engineering deck. There is a locator marker on each screen shows where that terminal stands around the reactor.
[list]
[*][b]Balance:[/b] take them off in opposite pairs, like the nuts on a car wheel: one, then the one straight across from it. The screen shows each opposite pair in its own color.  Start anywhere you like.
[*][b]Memorize:[/b] the screen flashes the order, one injector at a time, and draws it as a path of arrows. Remember it, go down and take them off in that order.
[*][b]Resonance:[/b] the right injector's handle lights blink exactly with the core's beat (brightest); the others blink a little out of step. The screen shows the beat as a wave.
[/list]
A wrong injector flashes the core red and raises the level; take the right one next and it drops back to blue.

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The plasma is radioactive up close, and touching it sets you on fire.
[*]Hold an injector, its pipe or its handle panel to hear the core through your suit; a controller rumbles with every beat.
[*]Pull the reactor out while the core plasma still burns and it explodes in the chamber. BIG BADA BOOM!
[*]Everything can be switched off or eased in the options menu, EXPANSE tab: no meltdown, no damage to you or the ship, which modes appear, and how fast it escalates.
[/list]


[size=5][b]Heavy parts come free gently[/b][/size]
The hull panels and large objects of these ships are built from a 3D model, as big curved and hollow pieces. The game treats every part as the solid shape around its mesh, so neighboring pieces overlap each other. While they are joined, that does not matter. The moment one is cut or pulled free, the game pushes the overlapping pieces apart at up to 10 meters per second, which throws a part of several tonnes faster than a tether can hold.

With this mod, that push depends on the part's mass:
[list]
[*]Parts of 5 tonnes or more are eased apart at 0.3 meters per second.
[*]Parts up to 100 kg keep the game's own speed, so small pieces still pop free.
[*]Parts in between fall on a smooth slide.
[/list]
Only the push between overlapping parts changes. The grapple, tethers, explosions and decompression move parts as before.


[size=5][b]Big rooms take time to pressurize[/b][/size]
The game fills and empties every room in about 5 seconds, whatever its size. These ships have one very large interior, and it is part of how the ship works that it takes time to fill and to vent.

With this mod:
[list]
[*]A room takes as long as the ship sets for it. Rooms left at the default behave as before.
[*]The atmosphere regulator's hiss and vent effect keep going for as long as the change lasts.
[*]Rooms connected by open doors change together and take the longest time among them.
[*]A hull breach still vents at the game's normal speed.
[/list]


[size=5][b]Ghost ships are more haunted[/b][/size]
The game's own haunting is kept as it is: doors, room pressure and electricity. On a ghost ship this mod adds to it, and like the game's haunting it gets worse as you destroy the Protomolecule nodes and stops with the last one.
[list]
[*][b]The ship rolls.[/b] Every few minutes it turns slowly about its long axis, pushing loose parts and you with it. Faster and more often as nodes are destroyed.
[*][b]Lights flicker and black out[/b] around one spot of the ship at a time.
[*][b]The nodes are radioactive.[/b] Get close and you lose health; radiation resistance counts.
[*][b]Your helmet light stutters[/b] near a node.
[*][b]The growth goes with the last node.[/b] Destroy them all and the ship is clean.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Hardspace: Shipbreaker
[*][url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases]BepInEx 5 (x64)[/url], not version 6 or above
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install BepInEx: extract it into the same folder as Shipbreaker.exe, run the game to the main menu, then quit.
[*]Download this mod and extract it into [b]BepInEx\plugins\[/b], so you end up with:
[code]Hardspace Shipbreaker\BepInEx\plugins\TheExpanse\me.kerballone.TheExpanse.dll[/code]
[/list]

To remove it, delete the [b]TheExpanse[/b] folder.


[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]
The settings file is created on first run:
[code]Hardspace Shipbreaker\BepInEx\config\me.kerballone.TheExpanse.cfg[/code]
Saving it while the game is running applies the change within a second.
[list]
[*][b]Enabled[/b] (default true): turns the whole mod on or off.
[*][b]GentleSeparation[/b] (default true): limit how fast overlapping parts are pushed apart when they separate, by mass.
[*][b]UsePressureTimes[/b] (default true): make each room's own pressurization and decompression time count.
[*][b]ExtendPressureEffects[/b] (default true): keep the regulator's hiss and vent effect going for the whole of a slowed pressure change.
[*][b]PressureEffectSeconds[/b] (default 2): how many seconds one play of the hiss and vent effect covers. Lower it if you notice pauses.
[*][b]Haunting[/b] section: each ghost-ship addition can be switched off, and its timing, speed, reach and damage tuned. Every setting is explained in the file.
[*][b]Reactor[/b] section: reactor control can be switched off, and the core's size and pulse, the escalation, the radiation, the fire, the instability threshold and the meltdown tuned.
[/list]


[size=5][b]Other custom ships[/b][/size]
Everything here applies to any custom ship. A ship author can make a room slow by setting [b]Pressurization Time[/b] and [b]Decompression Time[/b] on its room container, in seconds. Values of about 5 or less make no difference.


[size=5][b]Source[/b][/size]
Source and earlier versions are on GitHub: [url=https://github.com/KerballOne/ShipbreakerMods]KerballOne/ShipbreakerMods[/url]

